            .docNews: "1.5.0 — 2026-07-25\n\n• archive: drop an archive to unpack it right where it lives, or drop files to pack them — rar and 7z fetch a small helper once\n\n• documents in the converter: markdown, word files and pdfs turned into one another, all on this Mac\n\n• cleaning mode: one button locks the keyboard so you can wipe it; the mouse or a timer unlocks it\n\n• new screen tools, off until you enable them — an eyedropper and text or qr codes read into the clipboard history — plus a permissions tab here, listing what Hop can ask for and what it never does\n\n1.4.0 — 2026-07-22\n\n• tabs: the icon can hold up to four now, and modules drag freely between them\n\n• new modules: a time tracker — time per task, today and total, with a nudge past 8 hours — and a to-do list\n\n• the clipboard now remembers copied files by name; pasting drops the file right back\n\n• small status indicators on the icon, colored or monochrome; and, for anyone who'd like to, there's now a way to support hop\n\n1.3.1 — 2026-07-18\n\n• torrents: enabling downloads the engine right away — with live progress and follow-up choices right in the card\n\n• monitor: memory, disk and network figures now match Activity Monitor and Finder exactly\n\n• the download icon lights up only while a torrent is actually downloading\n\n1.3.0 — 2026-07-18\n\n• torrents: a lite client right in the panel — drop a .torrent or paste a magnet link, pick files, pause and seed; the engine downloads separately (~26 MB) when you enable the module\n\n• awake: the display stays on by default, and the closed-lid mode is fixed\n\n• window tiling hotkeys work right after launch\n\n• battery watts on discharge are computed correctly\n\n1.2.0 — 2026-07-15\n\n• the app relaunches itself after an update — and also updates right after your Mac wakes from sleep\n\n• memory: RAM and swap shown separately; the color follows macOS's own memory-pressure signal\n\n• the panel doesn't hold the keyboard anymore: typing goes